 "differences": [
  "The paper's mean key-press times (423.88, 388.08, 360.22 ms) and their SDs came out slightly different from the recorded times (423.86, 387.97, 360.26 ms; SD 87.44 for Reading against 87.73), so they were not used as checks; the paper's definition of the response time (and its handling of missing responses) is not given.",
  "The mean JND for Reading is 117.33 cents here against 117.32 in the paper (a 0.008 difference, more than printed rounding), so it was not used as a check.",
  "The article is the PLOS ONE version (2024, CC BY 4.0); the listed bioRxiv preprint (doi 10.1101/2023.10.11.561423) has the same title. The OSF data have no license of their own."
